core-text 20.0.0..21.0.0: `new_ui_font_for_language` passes its `f64` size to a `CGFloat` parameter

mrustc on powerpc-apple-darwin, core-text 20.1.0 (alacritty 0.17.0 via crossfont 0.8.1):

    core-text-20.1.0/src/font.rs:247:1 error:0: Type mismatch between f32 and f64

`CGFloat` is `f32` on 32-bit targets (core-graphics-types src/base.rs: `not(target_pointer_width =
"64")`), so `CTFontCreateUIFontForLanguage(ui_type, size, ..)` with `size: f64` does not type-check
there. Every other constructor in the file already converts with `as CGFloat`; core-text 21.1.0 does
it here too (and this is the only f64/CGFloat mix in the crate: `CTFontGetAdvancesForGlyphs` really
returns a C `double`). The function appeared in 20.0.0; the hunk applies to 20.0.0, 20.1.0 and 21.0.0.

--- a/src/font.rs
+++ b/src/font.rs
@@ -245,3 +245,3 @@
             ui_type,
-            size,
+            size as CGFloat,
             language
